 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps the callback so it runs inside the app context. You usually don't need to apply it yourself:\n\n- `@app.cli.command()` (`app.cli` is an `AppGroup`, set in `src/tessel/app.py:338`) applies it automatically. So does `@bundle.cli.command()` (`src/tessel/bundles.py:49`).\n- `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) does the wrapping. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n- For a plain `click` command, add `@needs_app_scope` explicitly.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (line 333) is what `needs_app_scope` calls (line 397). It then pushes `app.app_context()`.\n\n`TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level CLI group. It subclasses `AppGroup` but is a different thing.",
